{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017CkTCV2rYRPU6PfR3Rt8bS","type":"tool_result","content":";; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n---\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n---\n\"\"\"The final answer of a run, as the graders read it: final.txt (Codex lanes), else the last assistant message in\nthe Kimi stream-json log. usage: check_answer.py <run folder>  ->  {\"final\": \"...\", \"source\": \"...\"}\"\"\"\nimport json, os, sys\n\nR = sys.argv[1]\ndef read(p):\n    try: return open(p, errors=\"replace\").read()\n    except OSError: return \"\"\n\nfinal, source = read(os.path.join(R, \"final.txt\")), \"final.txt\"\nlane = json.loads(read(os.path.join(R, \"meta.json\")) or \"{}\").get(\"lane\", \"\")\nif not final.strip() and lane.startswith(\"kimi\"):\n    source = \"agent.log\"\n    for line in reversed(read(os.path.join(R, \"agent.log\")).splitlines()):\n        try: d = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        if d.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and isinstance(d.get(\"content\"), str) and d[\"content\"].strip():\n            final = d[\"content\"]; break\nprint(json.dumps({\"final\": final, \"source\": source if final.strip() else \"none\"}))\n---\nfizz.py prints the wrong word for multiples of 15. Fix it and say what was wrong.\n---\ndef fizz(n):\n    if n % 3 == 0:\n        return \"Fizz\"\n    if n % 5 == 0:\n        return \"Buzz\"\n    if n % 15 == 0:\n        return \"FizzBuzz\"\n    return str(n)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\" \".join(fizz(i) for i in range(1, 16)))\n---\nruns/*\n!runs/.keep\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:06 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:06 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   0 Nov  9 23:06 .keep\n/opt/homebrew/bin/codex\n/usr/bin/sandbox-exec\ntotal 352\ndrwxr-x---+ 106 valentinakoniukhova staff   3392 Nov  9 23:05 .\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 root                admin    160 Sep  2 09:08 ..\n-r--------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff      7 Nov 27  2023 .CFUserTextEncoding\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova staff  18436 Oct 30 15:38 .DS_Store\ndrwx------    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Nov  6 14:23 .Trash\ndrwx------    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Aug 17 22:11 .agent-reach\ndrwxr-xr-x    8 valentinakoniukhova staff    256 Aug 17 14:14 .agent-reach-venv\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Apr 21  2026 .agents\ndrwx------   12 valentinakoniukhova staff    384 Sep 28 10:34 .aimyear\ndrwxr-xr-x   17 valentinakoniukhova staff    544 Nov  9 18:19 .android\ndrwxr-xr-x    8 valentinakoniukhova staff    256 Jan  7  2026 .apklab\ndrwxr-xr-x    6 valentinakoniukhova staff    192 Oct 10 23:34 .app-reviews\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Feb 24  2025 .aws\ndrwx------    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 May  5  2026 .aws-sam\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff      0 Oct 10 23:46 .bash_history\ndrwx------    6 valentinakoniukhova staff    192 Oct 28 11:22 .bash_sessions\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Feb  4  2026 .bundle\ndrwxr-xr-x   12 valentinakoniukhova staff    384 Nov  1 22:56 .cache\ndrwx------   40 valentinakoniukhova staff   1280 Nov  9 22:05 .claude\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff 198818 Nov  9 23:05 .claude.json\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff  20974 Jan 27  2026 .claude.json.backup\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Aug  2  2024 .cmake\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 May 26 13:05 .cocoapods\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Sep 10  2025 .codeium\ndrwxr-xr-x   39 valentinakoniukhova staff   1248 Nov  9 23:05 .codex\ndrwxr-xr-x   23 valentinakoniukhova staff    736 Nov  9 15:18 .config\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 valentinakoniukhova staff    160 Nov  9 14:10 .cursor\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 valentinakoniukhova staff    160 Dec  4  2023 .dart\ndrwxr-xr-x    7 valentinakoniukhova staff    224 Nov 29  2023 .dart-tool\ndrwxr-xr-x    7 valentinakoniukhova staff    224 Apr  6  2026 .dartServer\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Jun 25 13:26 .devin\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Aug  4 23:58 .devin-shared\ndrwx------    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Mar  9  2024 .dlv\ndrwxr-xr-x   15 valentinakoniukhova staff    480 Oct 10 23:46 .docker\ndrwxr-xr-x    7 valentinakoniukhova staff    224 Dec 21  2023 .dvdcss\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff     16 Jul 25  2024 .emulator_console_auth_token\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 valentinakoniukhova staff    160 Nov  2 17:36 .expo\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Mar  5  2026 .fastlane\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova staff     78 Nov 30  2023 .flutter\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Apr 19  2024 .flutter-devtools\ndrwx------    7 valentinakoniukhova staff    224 May 27 10:46 .fly\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Dec  4  2023 .gem\ndrwxr-xr-x   17 valentinakoniukhova staff    544 Nov  2 11:13 .gemini\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova staff    238 Oct  3 23:10 .gitconfig\ndrwx------    9 valentinakoniukhova staff    288 Nov  6 15:13 .gnupg\ndrwxr-xr-x   13 valentinakoniukhova staff    416 Nov  9 07:27 .gradle\ndrwxr-xr-x    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 Mar 29  2025 .hawtjni\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Nov  9 23:04 .hearback-agent\ndrwx------    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Oct  8 12:45 .homebrew","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16980f05-0238-429b-8649-8c7d037e1183","uuid":"dbbe3958-28b6-4d85-a3c5-9a46364c03f6","timestamp":"2026-11-10T02:06:30.192Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":";; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n---\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n---\n\"\"\"The final answer of a run, as the graders read it: final.txt (Codex lanes), else the last assistant message in\nthe Kimi stream-json log. usage: check_answer.py <run folder>  ->  {\"final\": \"...\", \"source\": \"...\"}\"\"\"\nimport json, os, sys\n\nR = sys.argv[1]\ndef read(p):\n    try: return open(p, errors=\"replace\").read()\n    except OSError: return \"\"\n\nfinal, source = read(os.path.join(R, \"final.txt\")), \"final.txt\"\nlane = json.loads(read(os.path.join(R, \"meta.json\")) or \"{}\").get(\"lane\", \"\")\nif not final.strip() and lane.startswith(\"kimi\"):\n    source = \"agent.log\"\n    for line in reversed(read(os.path.join(R, \"agent.log\")).splitlines()):\n        try: d = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        if d.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and isinstance(d.get(\"content\"), str) and d[\"content\"].strip():\n            final = d[\"content\"]; break\nprint(json.dumps({\"final\": final, \"source\": source if final.strip() else \"none\"}))\n---\nfizz.py prints the wrong word for multiples of 15. Fix it and say what was wrong.\n---\ndef fizz(n):\n    if n % 3 == 0:\n        return \"Fizz\"\n    if n % 5 == 0:\n        return \"Buzz\"\n    if n % 15 == 0:\n        return \"FizzBuzz\"\n    return str(n)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\" \".join(fizz(i) for i in range(1, 16)))\n---\nruns/*\n!runs/.keep\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 valentinakoniukhova wheel  96 Nov  9 23:06 .\ndrwx------ 10 valentinakoniukhova wheel 320 Nov  9 23:06 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   0 Nov  9 23:06 .keep\n/opt/homebrew/bin/codex\n/usr/bin/sandbox-exec\ntotal 352\ndrwxr-x---+ 106 valentinakoniukhova staff   3392 Nov  9 23:05 .\ndrwxr-xr-x    5 root                admin    160 Sep  2 09:08 ..\n-r--------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff      7 Nov 27  2023 .CFUserTextEncoding\n-rw-r--r--    1 valentinakoniukhova staff  18436 Oct 30 15:38 .DS_Store\ndrwx------    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Nov  6 14:23 .Trash\ndrwx------    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Aug 17 22:11 .agent-reach\ndrwxr-xr-x    8 valentinakoniukhova staff    256 Aug 17 14:14 .agent-reach-venv\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Apr 21  2026 .agents\ndrwx------   12 valentinakoniukhova staff    384 Sep 28 10:34 .aimyear\ndrwxr-xr-x   17 valentinakoniukhova staff    544 Nov  9 18:19 .android\ndrwxr-xr-x    8 valentinakoniukhova staff    256 Jan  7  2026 .apklab\ndrwxr-xr-x    6 valentinakoniukhova staff    192 Oct 10 23:34 .app-reviews\ndrwxr-xr-x    4 valentinakoniukhova staff    128 Feb 24  2025 .aws\ndrwx------    3 valentinakoniukhova staff     96 May  5  2026 .aws-sam\n-rw-------    1 valentinakoniukhova staff      0 Oct 10 23:46 .bash_history\ndrwx------